                <pb facs="0158" n="74" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg74"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Conger.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-08-15"><hi rendition="#italic">August 15,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Acknowledging Mr. Conger’s telegram of August 14, Mr. Hay states that Prince
                    Ch’ing’s note is satisfactory; that the date for signing of completed treaty,
                    October 8, is absolute and not contingent on action of Russia. Mr. Conger is
                    directed to make this clear to Prince Ch’ing.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
